==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
{{etyl|xno|en}} and {{etyl|fro|en}} {{m|fro|arson}}, from the verb {{m|fro|ardoir}}, from {{etyl|la|en}} {{m|la|ardeō||to burn}}. Compare {{m|en|ardent}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|GA}} {{IPA|/ˈɑɹsən/|lang=en}}
* {{a|RP}} {{IPA|/ˈɑːsən/|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~|arsons}}

# {{lb|en|uncountable}} The [[crime]] of deliberately [[starting]] a [[fire]] with [[intent]] to [[cause]] [[damage]].
#* '''2006''', [[w:Paul Chadwick|Paul Chadwick]], ''Concrete: Killer Smile'', Part two, p.34
#*: '''Arson''', like we thought. three punks doused a car, lit it, and took off.
# {{lb|en|countable}} An instance of such a crime.

